# rule.forbid.workarounds

> **never work around a failure. diagnose it to its root cause and fix it there — and when the tool that failed is one you build, the failure IS the defect report.**

a **workaround** = any change to an input, a declaration, a config, or your own conduct that makes a failure go quiet while its cause stands. forbidden. a dream, a `.taken`, or a fulcrum that names one documents the defect and leaves it shipped.

## .why

- **it hides the report** — a failure is the one signal a design is wrong; a patch to the input silences it for the one party able to act
- **it recurs** — the cause stands, so every next edit, driver, and repo trips it and pays the diagnosis the first one skipped
- **it compounds** — each patch is locally sane; the cost shows only in sum, as hours

## 🔴 .the dogfooder

when the failed tool is the one under construction, there is no "human error". **every friction the builder hits, the next human hits too — without the context to patch around it.**

| the dogfooder thinks | what is true |
|---|---|
| *"my declaration was stale; I fixed it"* | the tool let a stale declaration exist. that is the defect |
| *"the refusal did its job"* | it fired at the costliest moment — a design defect |
| *"I'll note it as a follow-up"* | the follow-up is this round's work |

## .the bar — a pit of success

correct use asks **no questions and meets no friction**: the tool guides its caller, and the right move is the easy move. 🔴 **any friction is a critical defect, fixed immediately** — never a nitpick, follow-up, or dream.

- the wrong state is unreachable, or caught **once, at the cheapest moment**, with the **exact fix printed**
- soundness holds **by construction**, never by a list a human keeps in sync
- the cure ships with a clamp — red without it, green with it

## .the test

> **"did the cause of this failure change, or only my input to it?"** cause → a fix · input only → a workaround. stop; fix the cause.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you edit a declaration, glob, or config so a tool stops its refusal | why did the tool let that state exist, and refuse when it did? |
| one cause refuses many times — per lane, per file, per run | the check sits at the wrong moment. move it to the cheapest |
| a contract stays sound only while a human keeps a list in sync | the contract is the defect |
| you must read a doc or ask to use your own tool right | the tool does not guide. that friction is the defect |
| you write *"the tool did its job"* about a failure you just hit | 🔴 the sharpest cue |
| the same kind of failure shows up twice | 🔴 the first fix was a workaround |

blocker: an input, declaration, or config patched while the cause stands · a workaround recorded in place of a fix · a dogfooder's friction with their own tool left unfixed in the round it surfaced · one cause that refuses repeatedly, left in place · a contract that needs hand upkeep, left in place.

⇒ see also: `rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch` (learner, this repo — this closes its record-the-workaround door) · foreign, in peer repos: `rule.require.solve-at-cause` (ehmpathy/architect) · `rule.require.clamp-edge-cases` (ehmpathy/mechanic) · `rule.require.safe-by-default` (ehmpathy/ergonomist).
